      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles and how their corresponding sides are proportional.\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - The original isosceles triangle has side lengths 8 cm, 8 cm, and 10 cm.\n   - The longest side of the original triangle is 10 cm.\n   - The longest side of the similar triangle is 25 cm.\n\n2. **Determine the ratio of the corresponding sides:**\n   Since the triangles are similar, the ratio of the corresponding sides is the same. The ratio of the longest sides of the two triangles is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{25 \\text{ cm}}{10 \\text{ cm}} = 2.5\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the side lengths of the larger triangle:**\n   - The side length of the original triangle corresponding to the longest side of 10 cm in the larger triangle is:\n     \\[\n     8 \\text{ cm} \\times 2.5 = 20 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n   - The side length of the original triangle corresponding to the other two sides of 8 cm each in the larger triangle is:\n     \\[\n     8 \\text{ cm} \\times 2.5 = 20 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the perimeter of the larger triangle:**\n   The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of its side lengths. Therefore, the perimeter of the larger triangle is:\n   \\[\n   20 \\text{ cm} + 20 \\text{ cm} + 25 \\text{ cm} = 65 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of the larger triangle is \\(\\boxed{65}\\) cm.",
