    "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles. When two triangles are similar, their corresponding sides are proportional. This means that the ratio of the lengths of corresponding sides of the two triangles is the same.\n\nGiven:\n- The side lengths of the original isosceles triangle are 8 cm, 8 cm, and 10 cm.\n- The longest side of the similar triangle is 25 cm.\n\nWe need to find the perimeter of the larger triangle. Since the triangles are similar, the ratio of the longest sides of the two triangles is the same. The ratio of the longest sides is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{25 \\text{ cm}}{10 \\text{ cm}} = 2.5\n\\]\n\nThis means that each side of the larger triangle is 2.5 times the corresponding side of the original triangle. Therefore, the side lengths of the larger triangle are:\n\n- 8 cm * 2.5 = 20 cm\n- 8 cm * 2.5 = 20 cm\n- 25 cm (the longest side)\n\nThe perimeter of a triangle is the sum of the lengths of its sides. So, the perimeter of the larger triangle is:\n\n\\[\n20 \\text{ cm} + 20 \\text{ cm} + 25 \\text{ cm} = 65 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of the larger triangle is \\boxed{65} cm.",
